        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "bc2d6af0-5814-3b92-9866-c1179545e4d1",
                "word": "manosphère",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ea8f3482-62e9-47e1-a4fa-5dda8cdddee8",
                        "entry_id": "bc2d6af0-5814-3b92-9866-c1179545e4d1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "manosphères"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f50717e8-b52a-3623-b0f5-5069afda56f1",
                        "entry_id": "bc2d6af0-5814-3b92-9866-c1179545e4d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Communauté de sites internet et de réseaux sociaux misogynes dédiés aux hommes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neologism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4ab27f3-7934-4b6a-9d78-0483828de14b",
                                "sense_id": "f50717e8-b52a-3623-b0f5-5069afda56f1",
                                "text": "La manosphère est un réseau de sites Web et de forums en ligne. Une constellation de la misogynie. Protégés par l’anonymat, les hommes échangent des tuyaux, discutent stratégies de ­conquête, publient commentaires sexistes (ah, l’éternelle « polarité négative du cerveau féminin » !) ou revanchards (« Je viens de me taper une féminazie aux cheveux arc-en-ciel »)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d06cff92-e64d-4e59-86e8-57cfce82862d",
                                "sense_id": "f50717e8-b52a-3623-b0f5-5069afda56f1",
                                "text": "Une équipe de recherche américaine et britannique a d'ailleurs observé une radicalisation des discours en ligne dans les communautés de la manosphère. Selon l'étude, les groupes plus anciens comme les activistes des droits des hommes s'effacent au profit des plus violents comme les Mgtow et Incels."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cd3c0f86-67a7-4d1d-a796-c50fdb873cf7",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc2d6af0-5814-3b92-9866-c1179545e4d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "f50717e8-b52a-3623-b0f5-5069afda56f1",
                        "target_lang_word": "Manosphere",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "49a344ce-0e8e-41d0-84ec-142c4ead9e9c",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc2d6af0-5814-3b92-9866-c1179545e4d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "f50717e8-b52a-3623-b0f5-5069afda56f1",
                        "target_lang_word": "manosphere",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "manosphere",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "348b5b5e-04d7-3822-9dcc-55d31cd5dc78",
                                        "entry_id": "8db86000-46d5-37eb-95a4-7f123946aca8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The domain or totality of blogs and websites associated with the men's rights movement, the redpill movement or incels."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet",
                                            "neologism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df02fef7-38a5-4bd3-a71b-e37ba4877711",
                                                "sense_id": "348b5b5e-04d7-3822-9dcc-55d31cd5dc78",
                                                "text": "The Manosphere essentially is the counterpoint to the feminist doctrine (that empowers women at the expense of men). It is a free form community consisting primarily of men on the internet sharing experiences and thoughts with the intention of educating, empowering and improving the state of men and boys."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3814d738-8e3d-42e8-9dc9-401c817b4cb1",
                                                "sense_id": "348b5b5e-04d7-3822-9dcc-55d31cd5dc78",
                                                "text": "Incel is short for “involuntarily celibate”. The term rose to prominence because of its adoption by a subsection of the “manosphere”, a loose collection of movements united by misogyny that also includes some men’s rights activists, pick-up artists, and Mgtow/volcel – heterosexual men who refuse to have sex with women for political reasons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2088a215-ff30-4e4e-a1cb-02f39cbaafbb",
                                                "sense_id": "348b5b5e-04d7-3822-9dcc-55d31cd5dc78",
                                                "text": "The foundational tenet of taking the red pill is at the root of almost all the major manosphere groups we will look at in this book, including pickup artists, so-called Men's Rights Activists, and Men Going Their Own Way."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8608ede-34fb-4c2f-a6b0-2b74c9c96dbe",
                                                "sense_id": "348b5b5e-04d7-3822-9dcc-55d31cd5dc78",
                                                "text": "Maisie says that Danny entered the manosphere through the realm of self-help, which Cynthia Miller-Idriss, a sociology professor at American University who specializes in extremism, says is “a great example of how radicalization works.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
